    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "“Turestin” is a superb four-bedroom detached residence presented in exceptional showhouse condition, occupying one of Wexford Town's most sought-after and convenient residential addresses. Fronting the prestigious Newtown Road and set on an impressive site extending to approximately 0.49 acres, this outstanding home offers far more than first meets the eye.  Extensively upgraded and remodelled in recent years, the property seamlessly combines a traditional exterior with a stylish contemporary interior. At the heart of the home lies a spectacular triple-aspect open-plan kitchen, dining and living space, creating a bright and welcoming hub perfectly suited to modern family life and entertaining. The accommodation is generously proportioned throughout and comprises four spacious double bedrooms, including a luxurious principal suite complete with walk-in wardrobe and en-suite bathroom. A family shower room, utility room and an abundance of storage further enhance the practicality of this impressive residence. Enjoying scenic views towards Mount Leinster, the extensive grounds have been thoughtfully designed to offer a variety of outdoor relaxation and entertaining areas. The property also benefits from ample private parking, a feature rarely found in such a central town location.  The location is second to none. Less than one minute's drive from both the N25 and N11, the property is ideally positioned for commuters. Wexford General Hospital is within walking distance, while Wexford Town Centre, with its excellent selection of restaurants, cafés, shops, nightlife, train station and picturesque quays, is located less than 2km away. A host of renowned local amenities and beauty spots are also within easy reach, including the golden beaches of Curracloe and Rosslare Strand, Carrigfoyle Quarry and the magnificent Johnstown Castle, offering endless opportunities for recreation and enjoyment. Combining generous internal and external space, a prime town location and true turnkey condition, “Turestin” represents a rare opportunity to acquire a distinguished family home in one of Wexford's most desirable settings. Early viewing is highly recommended.  VIEWING HIGHLY RECOMMENDED."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway - (3.96m x 2.5m) & (5.8m x 1m), Laminate flooring, storage off, recessed lighting.\r\nKitchen/living/dining - (8m x 6.7m),Eye & Waist level units with island, tiled floor and splashback, solid fuel stove, recessed lighting, Triple aspect windows with views, french doors to outside.\r\nUtility - (3.3m x 1.8), Eye & Waist level units, plumbed for washing machine, tiled floor and splashback, door to outside.\r\nBedroom 1 - (4.2m x 3.6m), Laminate flooring, french door to outside.\r\nWalk in Wardrobe - (1.5m x 1.7m), Laminate flooring, fitted storage.\r\nEnsuite - (2.4m x 1.6m), WC, WHB, walk in shower, fully tiled, towel rail.\r\nBedroom 2 - (3.7m x 3.6m), Laminate flooring, double wardrobe, views.\r\nShower Room - (2.4m x 1.7m), WC, WHB, shower, fully tiled walls, laminate flooring.\r\nBedroom 3 - (3.7m x 4.3m), Laminate flooring, views.\r\nBedroom 4 - (3.1m x 2.9m),Laminate flooring.\r\n\r\nOutside: Spacious parking to the front, gardens to front and rear, patio area to the rear.\r\nServices: Electricity, mains water, private sewerage, oil fired central heating.\r\nBER: C Ber No: 110556180 Performance indicator: 199.19 Wh/m2/yr\r\nApply: Keane Auctioneers (053) 9123072\r\nViewing: Strictly by appointment with the sole selling agent.\r\nEircode: Y35H5K0"
